### When to Send Logs

**Progressive Logging (Recommended):**
1. After each screen completion
2. On session start (front page load)
3. On session end (final screen or abandonment)
4. Before page unload (if user closes browser)

**Implementation:**
- Use `fetch()` API to send logs to endpoint
- Queue logs locally if network fails
- Send queued logs when connection restored
- Include session_id in all requests to connect data

### Log Endpoint
Developer needs to provide:
- REST API endpoint URL (e.g., `https://your-domain.com/api/log`)
- Or webhook URL (e.g., Zapier, Make.com)
- Or Firebase Firestore configuration
- Or simple email webhook

### Human-Readable Log Format

After session completion, generate a timeline view:

```
=== DINNER INVITATION SESSION ===
Started: Feb 10, 2025 at 2:30 PM

--- JOURNEY TIMELINE ---

[00:00] 🏠 Front Page (5s)
        "Nom nom?" clicked

[00:05] 🎯 Control Quiz (13s)
        Dessert ⭐⭐⭐⭐ (4.8s hover)
        Selected: "Dessert decisions"

[00:18] 📅 Date Picker (10s)
        Saturday ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐ (8s hover) 💚
        Clicked: Saturday (direct, no mistakes!)

[00:28] 🎉 Success Screen (3s)

[00:31] 📋 Planning Quiz (34s)
        Smart casual ✓
        Spicy adventure ✓
