## Code Requirements

### HTML
- Semantic HTML5
- Single-page application (all screens in one HTML file)
- Screens hidden/shown with JavaScript
- Accessible (ARIA labels where needed)
- Meta tags for mobile viewport

### CSS
- Mobile-first responsive design
- CSS Grid or Flexbox for layouts
- CSS animations for transitions
- Hover states for interactive elements
- Media queries for responsiveness

### JavaScript
- Vanilla JS (no frameworks)
- Modular code structure:
  - `main.js` - Screen navigation, main flow
  - `logger.js` - All logging functionality
  - `chibi-controller.js` - Chibi expression changes
- Event listeners for all interactions
- Hover time tracking using timestamps
- Session storage for data persistence during session
- Clean, commented code

### Logger Module Requirements
```javascript
// logger.js should export:
- initSession() - Start new session with unique ID
- logScreenVisit(screenName) - Log when screen is entered
- logHover(element, duration) - Log hover events
- logClick(element) - Log click events
- logSelection(question, answer) - Log user selections
- logTextInput(field, value) - Log text field entries
- logNavigation(from, to) - Log back button usage
- sendLog() - Send accumulated log data to endpoint
- generateHumanReadableLog() - Create timeline format
```

### Chibi Controller Module Requirements
```javascript
// chibi-controller.js should export:
- setChibiExpression(expression) - Change chibi image
- handleDateHover(date) - Show appropriate expression for date
- animateChibi(animation) - Trigger animation (jump, dance, etc)
- resetChibi() - Return to neutral state
```

